BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-hip-nights-northwood-2026-11-27@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261121T143500Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261127T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261127T210000
SUMMARY:Nights in Northwood — Holiday Edition (Jam-X The Band) — FREE
LOCATION:Northwood Road\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33406
CATEGORIES:City events,Holiday in Paradise
DESCRIPTION:Holiday in Paradise signature event. Live music from Jam-X The Band (Top 40\, R&B\, Pop) on the NewDay USA stage. Open-air night market with more than 50 vendors (art\, fashion\, handmade goods\, vintage\, local food). Held on Black Friday\, the day before Small Business Saturday. Source: City of West Palm Beach news release "City Kicks Off the Holiday Season with Holiday in Paradise" (published 2026-11-09\, retrieved 2026-11-09): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/110926-HiP-kickoff Holiday in Paradise Presented by FPL runs Nov 27–Dec 31\, 2026 ("The Art of Holidays"). All signature events are free to attend. Sandi music and light shows nightly on the quarter hour 6–10 p.m. Dec 3–30 (adjusted during special events\; through midnight on New Year's Eve). Ferris wheel rides $5 per person during Sandi's show hours. More info: https://wpb.org/holiday Also listed as a 4th Friday quarterly event on the City's Nights in Northwood Village page (6-9 p.m.\, Northwood Road\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33406). The Mayor's Insider Newsletter describes it as a FREE event and says Jam-X The Band\, emerging from West Palm Beach\, blends pop\, neo soul\, funk\, reggae\, rock\, country\, and jazz. The November 20\, 2026 newsletter lists it as "NEXT Friday: Shop Local This Holiday Season! Nights in Northwood is Back with 50+ Vendors\," Friday\, November 27\, 6-9 p.m.\, free\, and points to wpb.org/NIN. The canonical event page retrieved 2026-11-21 still lists Friday\, November 27\, 2026\, 6-9:00 p.m.\, Northwood Road\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33406\, with Jam-X The Band and 50+ vendors. More info: https://wpb.org/NIN (canonical page\, retrieved 2026-11-14 and 2026-11-21): https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Nights-in-Northwood-Village Additional sources: City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Mayrs-Insider-Newsletter\; City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 20\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-20\, retrieved 2026-11-21): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/112026-Mayors-Insider-Newsletter
URL:https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/110926-HiP-kickoff
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-hip-vote-for-sandi-2026-11-30@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261124T143000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T120000
SUMMARY:Vote for Sandi (USA TODAY 10Best) deadline at noon
CATEGORIES:City events,Holiday in Paradise
DESCRIPTION:Holiday in Paradise has again been nominated as a USA TODAY 10Best "Best Public Holiday Lights Display." The City's Vote for Sandi page (retrieved 2026-11-24) says Sandi and friends won the national distinction in 2021 and asks the public to vote daily through Monday\, November 30 at noon. November 30\, 2026 is a Monday. This calendar entry marks that voting deadline\; it is not a public meeting or ticketed event. Vote: https://10best.usatoday.com/awards/holiday-in-paradise-west-palm-beach-florida/ (the "VOTE DAILY" link on the City page). A related-information link on the same page is https://10best.usatoday.com/qr/43562/. Source: Vote for Sandi page (retrieved 2026-11-24): https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Vote-for-Sandi\; linked from the Holiday in Paradise page: https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise.
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Vote-for-Sandi
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-hip-tree-lighting-2026-12-03@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261124T143000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261203T220000
SUMMARY:Clematis by Night Holiday Tree Lighting (Sandi debut) — FREE
LOCATION:West Palm Beach Waterfront\, 100 N. Clematis Street\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33401
CATEGORIES:City events,Holiday in Paradise
DESCRIPTION:Holiday in Paradise signature event and season debut of Sandi's synchronized music and light shows. The official Holiday Tree Lighting event page (retrieved 2026-11-24) lists Thursday\, December 3\, from 6-10:00 p.m.\, FREE on the West Palm Beach Waterfront\, 100 N. Clematis Street. Clematis by Night Holiday Tree Lighting featuring Phoenix5 (Soul\, Funk\, Rock\, Reggae) on the NewDay USA Stage. The page says Phoenix5\, twice named Best Live Performers by The Guide to Florida\, brings crowd favorites and mini tributes to artists including Prince\, Santana\, Bob Marley\, Stevie Wonder\, and Bruno Mars. Also joining: Officers & Gentlemen with the Rhythm Chicks\, with holiday favorites and hits from the '60s and '70s (military veterans and a polished vocal trio). The main Holiday Tree Lighting page prints the ensemble name as "Officers & Gentleman" (singular)\; the schedule subpage and the Nov 9\, 2026 news release print "Gentlemen." The event page says the celebration features FREE live music\, special entertainment\, photos with Santa\, and the Holiday Gift Boutique inside the Lake Pavilion and along Flagler Drive. The schedule subpage describes the boutique as inside the Lake Pavilion and does not mention Flagler Drive. PLEASE NOTE: the concert\, activities and the Holiday Boutique take place until 9:00 p.m.\; Sandi shows and rides on Ferris continue until 10 p.m. The Nov 9\, 2026 news release also listed live painting by Laura Serna 6-9 p.m.\, Santa and Mrs. Claus\, face painters\, and stilt walkers\; those details are not restated on the 2026-11-24 event pages and are kept here from that release. The City email "Holiday in Paradise presented by FPL~ Sandi Tree Lighting" (received Nov 23\, 2026) gave the December 3 date and downtown waterfront location but no time\; the time is taken from the official event page. That email also called Sandi a 35-ft sand tree\; none of the Holiday in Paradise pages retrieved 2026-11-24 state a height (an event-page image alt text calls Sandi a "holiday sand tree"). Source: City of West Palm Beach news release "City Kicks Off the Holiday Season with Holiday in Paradise" (published 2026-11-09\, retrieved 2026-11-09): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/110926-HiP-kickoff\; Holiday Tree Lighting event page (retrieved 2026-11-24): https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Holiday-Tree-Lighting-12.03.2026\; schedule listing and subpage (retrieved 2026-11-24): https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Schedule-of-Holiday-Events and https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Schedule-of-Holiday-Events/Clematis-by-Night-Holiday-Tree-LIghting\; City email "Holiday in Paradise presented by FPL~ Sandi Tree Lighting" (received Nov 23\, 2026). Holiday in Paradise Presented by FPL runs Nov 27-Dec 31\, 2026 ("The Art of Holidays"). More info: https://wpb.org/holiday (canonical page: https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise).
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Residents/Community-Events/Events/Holiday-in-Paradise/Holiday-Tree-Lighting-12.03.2026
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
