SUMMARY:Speaker Series: Tracking Kites - Film Screening & Director Q & A
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Boulevard\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Palm Beach County Environmental Resources Management\, Avian Research and Conservation Institute\, and the Palm Beach Zoo & Conservation Society team up to share how their research partnership has helped shape our understanding of the swallow-tailed kite and helped to inform successful management strategies for this incredible bird. Film followed by Q & A with Executive Producer Benji Studt. Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\, 10:00 a.m.–11:30 a.m. Ages: 15+. Cost: Free\, but space is limited. Reservations required. Check-in 15 mins before program start time at Nature Center. Come prepared: This will be a seated\, indoor presentation. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot. 561-804-4985. The official program page lists the end time as 11:30 a.m. (the earlier bulletin and the City email listed 11:00 a.m.).  Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Speaker-Series-Tracking-Kites-Film-Screening-112126\; earlier sources: City email "Upcoming Speakers and Film Screening!" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Grassy Waters Preserve bulletin (sent 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/FLWPB/bulletins/432ad0e
