DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261222T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261222T183000
SUMMARY:Full Moon Canoe
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:See the subtle changes that occur as Grassy Waters settles into night. Enjoy sunset over the marsh\, and then paddle under the glow of a full moon. Not for beginners - be sure to try one of our shorter daytime paddles first. Be sure to sign up with a partner\, canoes require two paddlers. Tuesday\, December 22\, 2026\, 4:00 p.m.–6:30 p.m. Ages: 15 and over (with at least one participating adult). Cost: $20 per person. Check in at the Nature Center 30 min prior to program start time. Come prepared: This tour is not intended for beginners. Wear clothes that can get wet and muddy. Bring a water bottle\, hat\, and sun protection. Binoculars and bug repellent also suggested. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Full-Moon-Canoe-122226
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Full-Moon-Canoe-122226
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-swamp-tromp-2026-12-26@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261226T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261226T113000
SUMMARY:Swamp Tromp
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Take a walk on the wild side during this hike through the cypress swamp. Be prepared to get wet and muddy! This hike is on a rugged trail that requires stepping over and ducking under vegetation and other obstacles. Expect knee-deep water levels. Saturday\, December 26\, 2026\, 10:00 a.m.–11:30 a.m. Ages: 8 and over (with participating adult). Cost: $10/adult\, $5/child. Check-in 15 mins before program start time at the Nature Center. Come prepared: Wear closed-toe shoes that can get wet and muddy. Shoes should fit tightly enough not to be pulled off by the mud (water shoes or old sneakers are best). Bring a water bottle\, hat\, sunscreen\, towel\, and change of clothes. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Swamp-Tromp-122626
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Swamp-Tromp-122626
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-marsh-critters-2026-12-27@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261227T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261227T113000
SUMMARY:Marsh Critters
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:The marsh comes alive in the palm of your hand as we discover the amazing aquatic insects and other small wonders that call the wetlands home. You’ll be knee deep in the marsh during this dipnetting adventure for the whole family! Sunday\, December 27\, 2026\, 10:00 a.m.–11:30 a.m. Ages: 5 and over (with participating adult). This program is intended for children with a participating parent/guardian. Cost: $10/child (accompanying adults free). Check in at the Nature Center 15 min prior to program start time. Come prepared: A parent/guardian must enter water with their child. Wear closed-toe shoes that can get wet and muddy and fit tightly enough not to be pulled off by the mud (water shoes or old sneakers are best). Wear sun protection and bring a water bottle\, towel\, and full change of clothes. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Marsh-Critters-122726
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Marsh-Critters-122726
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-animal-olympics-2026-12-28@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T130000
SUMMARY:Animal Olympics
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Join Grassy Waters Preserve naturalists to learn about the amazing adaptations of Everglades animals. Learn about these adaptations by competing through a series of hands-on activities to find out if you have what it takes to be an Everglades animal. Can you see as well as an owl? Are you as long as an alligator? Can you reach as far as a heron\, and more. Monday\, December 28\, 2026. Come anytime between 10:00 a.m.–1:00 p.m. Ages: All ages (with participating adult). Cost: FREE. Come prepared: This will be an indoor program. No Reservations Required. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Animal-Olympics-122826
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Animal-Olympics-122826
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-sunset-boardwalk-hike-2026-12-28@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T180000
SUMMARY:Sunset Boardwalk Hike
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a gentle\, late afternoon stroll to discover some of the fascinating flora and fauna of the Everglades. Then watch as flocks of wading birds fly into roost as the sun sets over the marsh. Monday\, December 28\, 2026\, 4:30 p.m.–6:00 p.m. Ages: 15 years and over (with participating adult). Cost: $10 per person. Check in at the Nature Center 15 min prior to program start time. Come prepared: Wear comfortable walking shoes and bring a reusable water bottle. Binoculars and bug spray are recommended. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Sunset-Boardwalk-Hike-122826
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Sunset-Boardwalk-Hike-122826
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-nocturnal-adventure-hike-2026-12-29@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261229T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261229T193000
SUMMARY:Nocturnal Adventure Hike
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Explore the Everglades at night during this family-friendly adventure. Start the evening by dissecting an owl pellet to learn more about these nocturnal birds and their amazing adaptations. Then\, enjoy a guided boardwalk scavenger hunt under the glow of the moon and stars as you learn more about the other nocturnal animals that call the Preserve home. Tuesday\, December 29\, 2026\, 6:00 p.m.–7:30 p.m. Ages: 5 and over (with participating adult). Cost: $10 per child (accompanying adults free). Check in 30 mins before program start time at the Nature Center. Come prepared: A parent / guardian must participate with their child. Wear comfortable\, closed-toe walking shoes and bring a refillable water bottle and bug repellent. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Nocturnal-Adventure-Hike-122926
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Nocturnal-Adventure-Hike-122926
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-gwp-canoe-cruise-2026-12-30@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261120T142119Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261230T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261230T113000
SUMMARY:Canoe Cruise
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Paddle your canoe through the shallow waters of the Everglades as you learn about the history and ecology of Grassy Waters on this guided tour. Be sure to sign up with a partner\, canoes require two paddlers. Wednesday\, December 30\, 2026\, 10:00 a.m.–11:30 a.m. Ages: 6-11 require two participating adults. Cost: $10 per adult\, $5 per child. Check in at the Nature Center 30 min prior to program start time. Come prepared: Wear clothes that can get wet and muddy. Bring a water bottle\, hat\, and sun protection. Reservations required\, space is limited. Please call the Nature Center to reserve a spot: 561-804-4985. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Canoe-Cruise-123026
URL:https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Canoe-Cruise-123026
END:VEVENT
