UID:wpb-svc-bulk-yard-waste-resume-2026-11-17@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T142600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Bulk and yard waste collection resumes (Briar Bay / Hamilton Bay)
LOCATION:Briar Bay\, Hamilton Bay\, and surrounding communities\, West Palm Beach\, FL
CATEGORIES:City services
DESCRIPTION:The City's Nov 12\, 2026 flood-response news release says bulk and yard waste collection will resume Tuesday\, November 17. Residents will not be charged for excess bulk or yard waste accumulated during the flooding-related service interruption. The Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13) specifies that collection will resume Tuesday\, November 17 in these communities\, referring to Briar Bay\, Hamilton Bay\, and neighboring areas. Regular residential garbage and recycling already resumed November 11\, with another round of collections November 12. Source: City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Mayrs-Insider-Newsletter\; City news release "West Palm Beach Provides Update on Ongoing Flood Response Efforts" (published 2026-11-12\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Flooding-Update
URL:https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Flooding-Update
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-svc-business-survey-deadline-2026-11-20@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T142600Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T170000
SUMMARY:West Palm Beach Business Survey deadline (TIP Strategies)
CATEGORIES:City services
DESCRIPTION:The City of West Palm Beach invites the City's business establishments to participate in a brief survey to help inform policies intended to guide the City's economic growth and resilience. The survey is being conducted on behalf of the City by TIP Strategies\, an Austin-based economic strategy firm. The newsletter states the survey is completely confidential\; no identifying information will be published\, and results will be provided in aggregate only. All survey responses must be completed by Friday\, November 20\, 2026\, at 5 p.m. This calendar entry marks that deadline\; it is not a public meeting. Take the survey: https://survey.zohopublic.com/zs/NhC5wV (title on the public survey page\, retrieved 2026-11-14: "West Palm Beach Business Survey"). Source: City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Mayrs-Insider-Newsletter
URL:https://survey.zohopublic.com/zs/NhC5wV
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-tmrw-city-usa-2027-04-13@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T142600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270413
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270415
SUMMARY:Tomorrow.City USA (Smart City Expo World Congress)
LOCATION:West Palm Beach\, FL
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow.City USA is the American flagship of Smart City Expo World Congress by Fira Barcelona. The event website title and body list April 13-14\, 2027\, in West Palm Beach. The Mayor's Insider Newsletter states the City will host the expo for the second consecutive year on those dates. The official visit page (retrieved 2026-11-14) describes a downtown conference and refers to "the venue" and "the convention center" but does not give a formal venue name or street address. Event site: https://tomorrowcity.us/ Source: City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Mayrs-Insider-Newsletter\; event website (retrieved 2026-11-14): https://tomorrowcity.us/
URL:https://tomorrowcity.us/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wpb-pr-winter-junior-soccer-2027@awormus.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T142600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270221
SUMMARY:Youth Winter / Spring Soccer League (Winter Junior Soccer 2027)
LOCATION:Howard Park Community Center\, 1302 Parker Avenue\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33401
CATEGORIES:Parks,Kids
DESCRIPTION:Registration for 2027 Winter Junior Soccer is open\, as stated in the Mayor's Insider Newsletter. On parks.wpb.org the program is listed as Youth Winter / Spring Soccer League (activity 211103). No registration deadline was listed on the parks activity pages retrieved 2026-11-14. Confirmed winter-session dates for Coed Soccer Ages 4 through 6 (211103-H1): January 9 through February 20\, 2027\, Saturdays 9:00-10:00 a.m.\, at Howard Park Community Center\, 1302 Parker Ave\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33401. Fees listed: $60 resident / $75 non-resident. The activity page asks participants to bring water\, a size 3 ball\, and cleats\, and notes volunteer coaches are needed. The same league also lists spring sections for ages 7-8\, 9-10 (Tue/Thu 6:00-7:00 p.m.) and ages 11-14 (Tue/Thu 7:00-8:30 p.m.) from March 9 through May 13\, 2027\, also at Howard Park Community Center. The newsletter also says you can register in person at any City of West Palm Beach Community Center or by calling (561) 804-4900 (TTY: 800-955-8771). Register online: https://parks.wpb.org/wbwsc/webtrac.wsc/search.html?module=AR&type=10 Source: City email "News & Events in the City of West Palm Beach" (Nov 13\, 2026)\; Mayor's Insider Newsletter (published 2026-11-13\, retrieved 2026-11-14): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-Mayrs-Insider-Newsletter\; parks activity listing (retrieved 2026-11-14): https://parks.wpb.org/wbwsc/webtrac.wsc/search.html?module=AR&type=10
URL:https://parks.wpb.org/wbwsc/webtrac.wsc/search.html?module=AR&type=10
END:VEVENT

